.Dd August 29, 2026
.Dt PS5DSENSE 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ps5dsense
.Nd Sony PlayStation 5 DualSense gamepad driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd device ps5dsense
.Cd device hid
.Cd device hidbus
.Cd device hidmap
.Cd device evdev
.Pp
In
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 :
.Cd dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_state
.Cd dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_color_r
.Cd dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_color_g
.Cd dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_color_b
.Cd dev.ps5dsense.%d.player_leds
.Pp
In
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Cd hw.hid.ps5dsense.debug
.Cd ps5dsense_load
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports the Sony PlayStation 5 DualSense gamepad
connected over USB,
and presents it to applications over the
.Sy evdev
interface.
.Pp
If the appropriate hardware is detected,
the driver will be loaded automatically by
.Xr devmatch 8 .
To load the driver manually at boot time, set the
.Va ps5dsense_load
variable to
.Ar YES
at the
.Xr loader 8
prompt, or add it to
.Xr loader.conf 5 .
.Pp
To give user applications access to the game controller,
allow user access to the
.Pa /dev/input/event*
nodes with inclusion of user in the
.Em games
group,
or with a
.Xr devfs.rules 5
ruleset.
.Pp
The microphone mute button is reported as
.Dv KEY_MICMUTE ;
unlike the vendor driver on other systems,
.Nm
does not mute the built-in microphone itself.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the following devices:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Sony DualSense wireless controller
.Pq USB product ID 0x0ce6
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following variables are available as
.Xr sysctl 8
variables:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_state
Lightbar state,
where 0 is off and
1 is on.
.It Va dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_color_r
Lightbar color,
red component.
.It Va dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_color_g
Lightbar color,
green component.
.It Va dev.ps5dsense.%d.led_color_b
Lightbar color,
blue component.
.It Va dev.ps5dsense.%d.player_leds
Player indicator LEDs,
where -1 is off and
0 to 4 select the player number.
.El
.Pp
The following variable is available as both
.Xr sysctl 8
variable and
.Xr loader 8
tunable:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va hw.hid.ps5dsense.debug
Debug output level,
where 0 is debugging disabled and
larger values increase debug message verbosity.
Default is 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/input/event*" -compact
.It Pa /dev/input/event*
input event device
.Pq Sy evdev
node
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hgame 4 ,
.Xr ps4dshock 4 ,
.Xr usbhid 4 ,
.Xr devfs.rules 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
The
.Nm
driver was written by
.An Christos Longros Aq Mt chris.longros@gmail.com .
.Sh BUGS
The
.Nm
driver does not support force-feedback events, haptic feedback or the
adaptive triggers.
.Pp
The touchpad and the motion sensors are not decoded.
The touchpad click is therefore not reported at all.
.Pp
Bluetooth operation is not supported.
